      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the base seven sum of the digits of the product of the base seven numbers \\( 24_7 \\) and \\( 30_7 \\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the base seven numbers to base ten:**\n\n   - Convert \\( 24_7 \\) to base ten:\n     \\[\n     24_7 = 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}\n     \\]\n\n   - Convert \\( 30_7 \\) to base ten:\n     \\[\n     30_7 = 3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21 + 0 = 21_{10}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Multiply the base ten equivalents:**\n\n   - Calculate \\( 18 \\times 21 \\):\n     \\[\n     18 \\times 21 = 378\n     \\]\n\n3. **Convert the product back to base seven:**\n\n   - To convert \\( 378_{10} \\) to base seven, we find the largest powers of 7 that fit into 378:\n     \\[\n     378 \\div 7^3 = 378 \\div 343 = 1 \\Rightarrow \\text{remainder } 378 - 343 = 35\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     35 \\div 7^2 = 35 \\div 49 = 0 \\Rightarrow \\text{remainder } 35\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     35 \\div 7^1 = 35 \\div 7 = 5 \\Rightarrow \\text{remainder } 35 - 35 = 0\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     0 \\div 7^0 = 0 \\Rightarrow \\text{remainder } 0\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, \\( 378_{10} \\) in base seven is:\n     \\[\n     155_7\n     \\]\n\n4. **Sum the digits of the base seven product:**\n\n   - The base seven number is \\( 155_7 \\). We sum the digits:\n     \\[\n     1 + 5 + 5 = 11\n     \\]\n\n5. **Convert the sum back to base seven (if necessary):**\n\n   - The sum \\( 11 \\) in base seven is the equivalent:\n     \\[\n     1 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 7 + 4 = 11_{10} = 25\n     \\]\n\nFinal Answer:\n\\boxed{25}",
