      "text": "We are tasked with finding the product of the base \\(7\\) numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\). The base seven numbers are converted to base ten for calculations:\n\n\\[\n24_7 = 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}\n\\]\n\\[\n30_7 = 3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 21 + 0 = 21_{10}\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute the product of these \\(18_{10}\\) and \\(21_{10}\\):\n\n\\[\n21_{10} \\times 18_{10} = 378_{10}\n\\]\n\nWe convert \\(378_{10}\\) back to base \\(7\\). To find this conversion, we determine how many complete powers of \\(7\\) fit into \\(378\\):\n\n\\[\n7^0 = 1\n\\]\n\\[\n7^1 = 7\n\\]\n\\[\n7^2 = 49\n\\]\n\\[\n7^3 = 343\n\\]\n\\[\n7^4 = 2401\n\\]\n\n\\(7^3 = 343\\) is greater than or equal to \\(378\\), so we do not include \\(7^4\\). The powers of \\(7\\) from \\(1\\) to \\(3^4\\) give us:\n\n\\[\n378 \\div 343 \\approx 1.093 \\implies 1 \\text{ \\(7^4\\)}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Remainder} = 378 - (1 \\cdot 343) = 378 - 343 = 35 \\text{ (in base 10)}\n\\]\n\nNow, convert \\(35\\) to base \\(7\\):\n\n\\[\n35 \\div 7 = 5 \\quad \\text{with a remainder of } 0\n\\]\n\nThus, \\(35_{10} = 50_7\\). Now we add the base seven numbers:\n\n\\[\n50_7 + 18_7\n\\]\n\nFirst, convert \\(18_7\\) to base seven for easier addition:\n\n\\[\n18_7 = 1 \\times 7^1 + 1 \\times 7^0 = 1 + 1 = 2_7\n\\]\n\nAdding \\(50_7\\) and \\(2_7\\):\n\n\\[\n50_7 + 2_7 = 52_7\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{52_7}\n\\]",
